        "texts": {
          "summary": "ResultsList (memo) re-renders with 200 ResultRow below it on every letter: prop `filters` is a new object each render with the same value, created at SearchPage.tsx:19. Wasted: about 20.2 ms per letter. Fix: wrap it in useMemo (React Compiler would do this automatically).",
          "why": "memo only skips a render when every prop is the same object as last time. `filters` looks the same, but it's a new object on every render, so ResultsList and everything below it re-renders for nothing.",
          "line": "`filters={{ sort: 'recent', tags }}` at SearchPage.tsx:19.",
          "fix": "Wrap it in useMemo so ResultsList gets the same object until its contents change: `const filters = useMemo(() => ({ sort: 'recent', tags }), [tags]);`, then pass `filters={filters}`. React Compiler would do this automatically."
        },
        "rank": 1
      },
