        "texts": {
          "summary": "SearchBox sets state inside useEffect (SearchBox.tsx:10): one extra update per letter (under 0.1 ms). Fix: compute charCount during render: `const charCount = value.length;`. React Compiler doesn't fix this one.",
          "why": "SearchBox copies a value into state inside useEffect. React renders SearchBox, runs the effect, and then has to render it again with the new charCount: two updates where one would do.",
          "line": "`setCharCount(value.length)` at SearchBox.tsx:10.",
          "fix": "Compute `charCount` during render instead: `const charCount = value.length;`, and remove its useState and the useEffect. React Compiler doesn't fix this one."
